# Pi workflow reference

Env-specific facts; if behavior seems changed, verify against the source repo and update its
template in the chezmoi repo. Decisions: the repo's `docs/decisions.md`.

## Launch and pins

- The managed `pi` zsh function runs the lockfile-pinned CLI (currently {{ index (fromJson (include "package.json")).dependencies "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent" }}, one
  pin with the extensions and worker SDK) with native tools and ambient extensions
  off; a binary run outside it bypasses the workflow. Sessions load the applied
  `~/.pi/agent`, so a source edit needs `chezmoi apply`. Sign in through Pi's
  OpenAI subscription login; do not import another harness's auth files.

## Models

- Default: `{{ .agents.pi.defaults.provider }}/{{ index .subagent_tiers.pi .agents.pi.defaults.tier }}`, {{ .agents.pi.defaults.reasoning_effort }} reasoning.
- The approval classifier (MCP calls, remote-mutating shell verbs, unsandboxed requests)
{{- $cls := .agents.pi.defaults.classifier }}{{ $clsModel := index .subagent_tiers.pi $cls.tier }}
  runs two tool-less stages: `{{ $clsModel }}` at {{ $cls.filter_effort }} reasoning screens each reviewed action; anything
  but allow goes to `{{ $clsModel }}` at {{ $cls.judge_effort }} reasoning on the same prompt, whose verdict is final.
- Specialist roles, from `subagents` in agents.yaml (`docs/decisions.md` records each why):

| role | model | reasoning |
|---|---|---|
{{ range $name, $role := includeTemplate "pi-roles" (dict "root" .) | fromJson -}}
| {{ $name }} | `{{ $role.model }}` | {{ $role.thinking }} |
{{ end }}
- `workflow/children.mjs` rejects frontier children. Every tier pin is in the SDK's subscription
  catalog (the startup probe checks each); if one is dropped, fail unavailable, not an alias or API billing.
- All models draw one plan allowance at their own rate ([live rate card](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/pricing));
  API task cost is not Pro allowance; compare completed tasks including retries.
{{- $cw := list }}{{ range $tier, $n := .agents.pi.defaults.context_window }}{{ $cw = append $cw (printf "%s (%v tokens)" $tier $n) }}{{ end }}
- Context window: pinned for {{ $cw | join ", " }}; other tiers keep pi's catalog figure.
  A `context_length_exceeded` below the pin means the subscription limit moved.

## Specialists and skills

- Specialists under `~/.pi/agent/agents` render from the shared roster with an
  explicit model, tool list and policy extension; read-only ones stay read-only in
  execution. Only `general-purpose` may launch children, to Claude Code's depth.
{{- $sub := include "private_dot_pi/agent/extensions/subagent/config.json" | fromJson }}
- Children run in the background, sharing the root policy, up to {{ .agents.pi.child_limit }} at once
  across the tree; they start fresh with no channel back (intercom off);
  batch independent launches.
- Scripts/chains, role overrides, revival and mutating management are refused; status, stop,
  interrupt and steer work. Runs stop after {{ div $sub.timeoutMs 60000 }} minutes, with a checkpoint steer
  {{ div $sub.checkpointBeforeDeadlineMs 60000 }} minutes before.
- Skills are listed in the root's system prompt and load by `/skill:name` or on the model's own
  read. A child's MCP reach is its role's tool list; the policy refuses a tool outside it.

## Web search

{{ includeTemplate "web-search.md" (dict) | trim }}
- `web_search` is the pinned `pi-web-search` plugin: OpenAI's server-side search
  on the ChatGPT-subscription endpoint model calls use — no extra credential or
  network path, and the provider's own terms grey zone. Each search is one extra
  request on the usage windows, at the {{ .agents.pi.search_tier }} tier set in `~/.pi/agent/web-search.json`.
  Roles with Claude's `WebSearch` get it.
- Read a page with `web_fetch`: fetched in-process (public hosts only; a redirect to
  another host comes back to fetch again), converted to markdown, and the {{ .agents.pi.search_tier }} tier
  answers the prompt from it. Roles with Claude's `WebFetch` get it.
- Use Playwright for pages that need JavaScript.

## MCP and code intelligence

- MCP tools are pi's native `mcp__<server>__<tool>` (e.g. `mcp__context7__query-docs`),
  called directly. The root's MCP tools are all deferred: `tool_search` finds and
  loads them for the calls that follow. A child is declared exactly the MCP tools
  its role lists.
- MCP servers other than Playwright (see `sandbox.md`) run inside SRT; Node servers
  use `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` so fetch follows the sandbox proxy. If every call
  fails with `fetch failed`, check that setting, then the allowed domains.
- No LSP: diagnostics come from project toolchains via `workspace_bash` (`tsc --noEmit`,
  `go vet`, pyright, linters). Claude's proprietary plugins and cloud services: use Claude.
